<figure class="cache-figure" data-memory-encoding>
 <p class="figure-title">One more field, a different representation</p>
 <label><input type="checkbox" data-extra /> Add field 513</label>
 <div class="encoding-layout" data-layout><small data-layout-label>Compact sequence · three representative entries</small><div class="encoding-entries">{[0,1,2].map(i=><div class="encoding-entry"><span class="encoding-bucket" aria-hidden="true">bucket ↓</span><code>f{i} · small</code></div>)}</div></div>
 <p class="figure-note">Measured on Redis 8.2.2 · 64-bit arm64 macOS · libc allocator</p>
 <div class="memory-encoding-row"><span>Allocated bytes</span><div class="memory-encoding-track"><span data-bar></span></div></div>
 <div class="memory-encoding-axis"><span>0</span><span>37,008 bytes</span></div>
 <div class="cache-stat-row memory-encoding-stats"><div><strong data-fields>512</strong><span>fields</span></div><div><strong data-bytes>7,200</strong><span>MEMORY USAGE bytes</span></div><div><strong data-encoding>listpack</strong><span>OBJECT ENCODING</span></div></div>
 <p class="explanation" data-explanation aria-live="polite"></p>
 <figcaption>Every field has a short name and the value “small”. This instance's hash listpack limits were 512 entries and 64 bytes per field/value. Toggling compares two recorded states; it does not remove a field from an already-converted hash or predict conversion back. The three-entry layout is schematic, not a byte-level memory diagram. Allocation numbers depend on build, allocator and data.</figcaption>
</figure>
<script>
import {encodingSamples} from '../../lib/caching/memory.mjs';
document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-memory-encoding]').forEach(root=>{const input=root.querySelector<HTMLInputElement>('[data-extra]')!;const render=()=>{const s=encodingSamples[Number(input.checked)];root.querySelector('[data-layout]')!.classList.toggle('table-layout',input.checked);root.querySelector('[data-layout-label]')!.textContent=input.checked?'Hash table · buckets locate separate entries':'Compact sequence · three representative entries';root.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-bar]')!.style.width=`${s.bytes/37008*100}%`;for(const key of['fields','bytes','encoding'])root.querySelector(`[data-${key}]`)!.textContent=typeof s[key]==='number'?s[key].toLocaleString('en-GB'):s[key];root.querySelector('[data-explanation]')!.textContent=input.checked?'The extra field crosses the encoding threshold. Reported allocation rises by 29,808 bytes; most of that increase is not the new field’s text.':'The compact listpack holds 512 fields in 7,200 reported bytes. Add one field to cross this instance’s configured threshold.';};input.onchange=render;render();});
</script>
